; Template for Game/Config/Windows/WindowsEngine.ini (docs/03 §6.4). That file is git-ignored and must never be committed.
; Easiest: double-click Tools\SetupEOS.bat, it creates the file and asks for the ClientSecret.
; By hand: copy this file, drop ".example" from the name, replace HIER_EINTRAGEN with the ClientSecret from the
; Epic Developer Portal. Only the PC that packages the game needs it; players never do.
; The non-secret IDs (ProductId, SandboxId, DeploymentId, ClientId) are in Game/Config/DefaultEngine.ini.
; Comments in .ini files always on their own line.
[EOSSDK.Platform.HCDev]
ClientSecret=HIER_EINTRAGEN
